## Loaded flake found and root-caused during round 2
recovery/e2e failure failed once in 35 loaded runs at local-crash: screen/exact true, no gap.
Cause (fixture drill): the checkpoint took whatever bytes had arrived when MARK was seen; under load the chunk with MARK
could already extend past the holder's retained start (8312), so no gap existed. Fix: the writer blocks on a FIFO right
after MARK and the drill releases it only after checkpointing, so the checkpoint is exactly 1244 and the gap 1244->8312,
both now pinned literally.

## Clean control after the fix, same load (taskset -c 0-1, 8 busy loops)
recovery/e2e x25 + remote/e2e x25 --case all: PASS=50 FAIL=0
